WEBVTT

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:03.370
My passionate Idol Activities,

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:06.310
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.820
Get over here, Ichigo.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.240
It's about to start.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:13.860
Already?

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.160
It starts at 7:30, 25 seconds.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:23.250
Only five more seconds. 
Four, three, two, one...

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:25.560
There it is!

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.590
Stylish Thieves Swallowtail.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:32.340
Currently playing at theaters across the country.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.060
Recording complete.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:36.900
You were recording it?

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:37.890
Of course.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:41.250
It's your very first commercial, after all!

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.550
Even though it was such a short commercial,

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:49.830
you can feel the passion of the staff who made it and wanted to promote their movie to everyone.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.360
Do you know what that means?

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:53.810
What?

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:57.410
It means that they have great 
expectations of you as a rising star.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.850
Nice analysis...

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.620
But is that really true?

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.870
There's no question. In fact, 
there's no question it'll make huge waves! {fuck, fuck everything}

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:08.370
I guess you're never wrong.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:10.610
I'm getting jittery with excitement!

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:12.510
There's only one place we can go now.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:13.850
Where's that?

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:17.290
Do you have to even ask? The movie theaters!

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.270
Hi, signalize!

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:41.650
The answer lies on the other side of the sky

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:41.630
kotae wa motto takai sora no kanata

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.520
No, that's wrong

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.520
iie chigau yo

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:48.900
I can see with my eyes that it's at the end of the Earth

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:48.900
boku no me ni mo mieta chi no hate

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.690
Do that signalize!

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:55.870
Something's starting to bubble up

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:55.870
hageshiku natta mune no atsui powaa

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.830
From the burning power in my raging heart

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.830
sou da minagiru nanika ga

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.370
So I'll believe in the present

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.370
dakara ima wo shinjite

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:08.540
And start today since it's more than a faint desire

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:08.540
hajimeyou tada no akogare ja nai

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:09.880
Chance for me

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:15.180
Dreams can make even the harshest nightmare pleasant

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:15.180
zankoku na yume ga yume de yume ni narunda

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:19.390
It's just another challenge on the way

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:19.390
hora chousen matteru yo

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:24.310
Where are we headed?

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:24.310
kimi to mukau basho wa doko darou

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:28.060
Into a brilliant hope

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:28.060
mabushii kibou no naka e

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:35.320
Where do we want to go? Let's go find it right now

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:35.320
nozomu basho wa doko darou sagashi ni ikou yo shuppatsu da

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:38.700
Where we're headed

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:38.700
mukau basho wa mirai no

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:42.580
is into our hopes for the future

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:42.580
bokura no kibou no naka ni

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:49.920
Our destination is the future, the light is our signal Let's go, go!

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:49.920
nozomu basho wa mirai no kagayaki ga aizu let's go, go

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:01.110
And done.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.870
It's a bit risky to actually go see your own movie, though.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:08.450
You don't often land the lead role 
so I want to see it normally.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.500
Though it looks like she'll be <i>normally</i> found out.

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:18.630
Love you!

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.240
Hold it right there.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:26.560
If they find out that the lead actresses have come to see the movie, they won't keep quiet about it.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.560
That in itself would cause problems for the movie theater.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:30.890
Okay...

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:34.510
But we disguised ourselves, so aren't we safe?

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:38.270
Let's make your "disguise" a bit less flashy.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:43.270
When celebrities try to cover themselves up too much, it often has the opposite effect.

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:44.660
Thanks.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.660
Idols themselves are already prone to drawing attention.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.190
Their scent gives them away.

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:51.660
An idol's scent?

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.320
Let's get going.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:05.910
Here.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:10.600
Oh yeah, I forgot that I already had a ticket from the staff.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.180
Sorry I made you waste money.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:17.380
I got it because I wanted to.  I got one to use today, one to store, and one to look at later.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:20.230
I keep the limited preorder tickets in a special folder too.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:25.740
Raichi, do you want salted or caramel popcorn?

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.880
Are you trying to decide by smell?

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:35.510
That's not it. Don't you smell an idol around here?

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:48.580
It's about to start.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:49.450
Yeah.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.480
There they are!

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:55.230
On the roof!

00:04:55.690 --> 00:05:00.230
Guided by the scent of adventure, we are the gracefully fluttering butterflies!

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:04.870
Stylish Thieves Swallowtail! 
We fly off in search of treasure!

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.740
Fluttering forever more!

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.490
Don't let them get away!

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:11.620
Do you really think you can catch us?

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:13.240
It's Onee-chan!

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:16.040
She's a wonderful new-age Swallowtail.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.630
I wonder if Aoi-neesan will make a guest appearance?

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:19.820
Wait!

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:22.650
As if we'd ever wait for you!

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.470
That was really engaging.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:29.420
Yeah.

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:34.980
That was great! It was <i>the</i> best!

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.140
Thanks!

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:39.450
All your hard work until now finally paid off.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:40.360
I know!

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:44.490
There's still a long way to go on 
the path to becoming an idol.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:45.650
Let's go.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:50.250
The Beautiful Blade appeared! Love you!

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.230
She's walking like she's on the runway in a fashion show.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:59.420
Her aura's overflowing just from walking around.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:04.380
Ran-san!

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:06.380
Raichi.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:08.040
You were here?

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:09.340
Onee-chan.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.600
And Aoi-neesan too! Oh yeah!

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:15.470
P-Please accept this.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:18.350
It's for White Day.

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:20.690
Thanks.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.360
Rare...

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:26.150
You bet. Have you been carrying this everywhere?

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:29.520
Yes! I had to be ready for whenever I'd meet you.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:30.360
Mama.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:32.370
Hello, girls.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:33.860
Nice to see you again.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:34.850
Good afternoon.

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:38.370
It's Ichigo-tan's mom! Love you!

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:40.580
Why thank you very much.

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:43.880
It's another rare moment!

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.380
What did you think of the movie?

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:49.510
You were both wonderful as Swallowtail.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:51.510
Really?

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.400
I'm so glad!

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:56.930
But still, good job realizing we were here.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.490
Yeah, we were even in disguise. {really? really? you think your family won't notice you without your bow? you really are Takamina}

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:02.970
I can't really explain it, but I felt like I smelled the scent of an idol around here.

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:05.400
Huh? You can sniff out idols?

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.640
You're not half bad, Raichi. {...}

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:08.590
Nee-san?

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:10.700
Being able to sense the scent of idols

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:14.490
is the proof that you're proceeding nicely along the path to becoming a true idol fan.

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:19.770
Th-Thank you! It's like I can tell that each and every idol has her own unique scent!

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:20.710
That's right!

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:22.040
I did it!

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.960
Unique scents?

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:26.910
Yeah. Aoi-neesan's is...

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.420
A sparkly scent!

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:31.430
Really?

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:36.250
Ran-san's is like a flying butterfly. {fluttering has the same issue with syllable overlap}

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:37.230
She does!

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:38.470
What's <i>that</i> smell like?

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.580
And Otome-san has...

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:43.780
a sweet scent like candy.

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:44.810
She does!

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:49.110
Amazing. So it <i>is</i> true that idols all have their own scents.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.310
What about me?

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:53.110
Yours is...

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:04.330
Cafe au lait?

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.950
I just drank that earlier...

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:07.200
You must've spilled some.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.260
Wipe yourself properly.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:15.140
I can't really smell anything from you. Weird...

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.300
Huh?

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:25.520
Did you spill some there too?

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:26.400
No,

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:30.480
I was just wondering why I'm the only one who doesn't smell like an idol.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:35.160
Even though it's called that, 
it's not like you actually have a scent.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:39.690
When we say an idol's "scent", 
we really mean her aura.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:41.160
Her aura?

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.030
Haven't you felt it before?

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:45.160
It's like seeing an idol's radiance.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:48.040
I've felt it from Mizuki-chan before.

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:50.430
Right? That's an aura.

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:53.800
You don't see auras with your eyes—
you feel them with your heart. {oh really?}

00:08:57.310 --> 00:08:59.560
Well? Can you feel my aura?

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:04.200
It's not like it'll happen just from 
doing the same thing as Mizuki-san.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:05.690
I guess not...

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:08.000
How can I make it appear?

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:13.940
Hey honeys!

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:16.950
Rolling, rolling, rolling!

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:21.330
All of this rolling can mean only one thing!

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:24.770
A job offer for you honeys has come in.

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:25.850
Yeah!

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:29.540
We've received an offer for a public concert.

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:31.750
We did it!

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:32.620
Yeah.

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:34.760
You mean we can perform without auditioning?

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:39.620
That's right. The sponsors have 
been watching your auditions

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:42.070
and specifically asked for you three.

00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:45.490
You've been making a lot of 
appearances elsewhere as well.

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:46.570
That's right.

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:51.320
Kiriya has been getting increasing screentime in the TV drama "Naughty Detectives".

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:55.190
Shibuki has regular work as a model.

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:57.050
As for Hoshimiya...

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:01.280
the number of viewers on the release day of your movie was outstanding. {Release day! That has nothing to do with how well she acted! That's a measure of hype!}

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:04.960
This is a critical moment for all three of you.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:07.210
Perform your Aikatsu with everything you've got.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.320
Yes.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:11.670
And Hoshimiya, in order to promote your movie,

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:14.680
there's an additional offer to appear on the radio.

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:19.590
You'll be able to speak a lot on the radio and promote yourself even more.

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:23.980
Arisugawa is doing promotional specials on TV,

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:25.610
so you need to do your fair share as well.

00:10:25.610 --> 00:10:26.520
I will.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:29.810
Let's do this.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:30.620
Right.

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:31.710
You bet.

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:34.940
One, two—

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:41.470
<i>Alright! All I've gotta do now is learn how to let my aura out like Aoi and Ran!</i>

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:59.230
This garlic's delicious.

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:01.390
Yurika-sama, would you like a bite?

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:07.520
You have the gall to try and feed a vampire 
garlic? I'll suck your blood.

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:11.070
Then how about a tomato?

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:14.690
I suppose Yurika-sama will accept your offering.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:16.900
Love you!

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:20.910
That looks delicious!

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:24.410
<i>Everyone's able to let their aura out so easily.</i>

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:39.090
<i>And Mizuki-san's seems to </i>always<i> be out.</i>

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:49.100
Aikatsu!

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:52.550
What's she doing?

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:54.260
She's training her aura.

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:57.860
She says she has to work on her own to catch up to us.

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:59.860
Aikatsu!

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.870
It's not like it's a bad thing...

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:07.370
I've felt Ichigo's scent since the very beginning.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:10.640
The only one who hasn't realized it is Ichigo herself.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:14.380
The time!

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.940
Aoi, Ran, I'm off to the radio show.

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:19.490
Have a safe trip.

00:12:19.490 --> 00:12:21.260
See you at the concert.

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:25.540
What idols are you following these days?

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:27.100
I'd say Kanzaki Mizuki.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:28.240
Me too.

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:34.020
<i>I wonder if I really don't give off an aura.</i>

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:36.980
Good afternoon!

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:40.280
I mean, good morning.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.280
I'll be in your care.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.730
Same here.

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:46.620
If there's something you don't 
understand, don't hesitate to ask.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:48.750
Thank you, I will.

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:51.580
So I've heard that this program's actually really popular.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:55.480
Thanks to your appearance, we're expecting tens of thousands of listeners today.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:57.000
Tens of thousands?!

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:01.010
<i>O-Oh no... I've got butterflies in my stomach.</i>

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:05.930
And now it's time for radio!

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:08.210
You're listening to "Idol Station".

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:12.700
Our guest today is from the movie getting rave reviews, "Stylish Thief Swallowtail: The Movie"—

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:15.170
here's Hoshimiya Ichigo-chan!

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:17.100
G-Good evening!

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:20.580
I-I mean good mor—good afternoon!

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:23.110
Th-The guest is Onee-chan?!

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:24.750
I mean good afternoon!

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:27.110
I'm sorry, I know it's only noon...

00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:29.760
That's freshness for you.

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:33.020
Ichigo-chan made her debut in October of last year.

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:36.370
Since then, you've paired up with Kanzaki Mizuki-chan

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:40.150
and oh, you cut down a tree last Christmas, right?

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:43.450
That time was amazing. What 
happened to the tree after that? {yeah seriously, where is it?}

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:45.410
<i>My heart's beating out of my chest.</i>

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:48.010
Ichigo-chan?

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:49.470
Yes?

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:53.640
Looks like you were flying 
away somewhere just now.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.110
Huh? Flying away?

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:59.230
Now then, we'll be continuing our 
talk after the commercial break.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:00.860
Everyone, listen in next week too!

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:11.330
I'm sorry. After I heard about how many people would be listening, I just got so nervous...

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:14.360
My bad, guess I said a bit too much.

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:15.580
Not at all.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:18.740
But you know, there's really nothing to be afraid of.

00:14:18.740 --> 00:14:20.000
Look at your mic.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:26.780
There may be more people listening 
than there are holes in that mic.

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:31.140
However, all you have to do is talk 
to just a single one of those holes.

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:33.650
If you do, I'm sure your feelings will get across.

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:38.100
It's time for the Idol Advice Corner! {if you don't like it change it back}

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:42.400
Our guest Hoshimiya Ichigo will listen 
to any worries you may have.

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:40.010
Think she'll be okay?

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:41.520
Don't worry, she'll do great.

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:45.270
This one's from a regular.

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:47.080
Ichigo-chan, I leave it to you.

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:48.530
O-Okay.

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:51.780
<i>A single hole.</i>

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:54.270
<i>To a single person...</i>

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:59.040
This is a letter from pen name Raichingale.{???}

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:02.790
Thank you for your mail. Raichingale's concern is...

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:02.790
It's my letter!

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:05.840
"I really love Kiriya Aoi-san."

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:07.480
Same as me!

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:10.950
"If I were to write everything I like 
about her, first is her Aikatsu—

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:13.220
but no, I'd just run out of space."

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:18.930
Aoi's my best friend, so this really 
makes me happy. Now then—

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:18.930
She knows it's me! She definitely knows it's me!

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.400
"Here's my worry:

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:26.570
I'm so preoccupied with Aoi-san that I sometimes get worried about my own future.

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:30.790
Sometimes I feel like I have to hurry up and find my own dream, like she has.

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:34.330
Is it really okay for me to keep 
chasing after Aoi-san like this?"

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:38.080
Of course I think you should.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:42.330
I myself became an idol because I
 was chasing after Kanzaki Mizuki-san.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:46.360
Although it may seem that I decided on my dream just because of Mizuki-san,

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:48.920
once I actually started my Aikatsu,

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:51.260
I suddenly found myself overflowing with dreams.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:55.960
Like wanting to be an idol that can make everyone happy.

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:57.680
Like wanting to always try my best

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:00.680
in Aikatsu alongside Aoi and Ran forever...

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:06.680
That's why I'm sure that if you continue doing the things you like, you're sure to find your own dream.

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:11.050
That's what I can say now because 
of the time I've put into Aikatsu.

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:16.890
So to Raichingale-san,

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:19.910
I hope that you'll always continue following after Aoi, okay?

00:16:22.030 --> 00:16:24.560
Onee-chan's really an idol...

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:26.290
Ichigo-chan.

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:28.290
You're a bit close to the mic. {lol, forcing your aura through the mic} {well there are holes in it}

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:33.800
That's right. It's important to always follow your dreams.

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:36.850
Raichingale-san, you can do it.

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:38.810
Now let's move on to the next message.

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:43.060
Ichigo, we heard you on the radio.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:44.310
Thanks.

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:45.910
Your aura was flowing out.

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:47.070
Really?

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:47.970
Yeah.

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:50.440
I didn't realize it at all.

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:54.520
An aura isn't something that you 
consciously try to produce.

00:16:54.520 --> 00:16:58.450
It's something felt by those 
around you as they watch you.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:03.280
In other words, the most important thing is to be aware of who you are as an idol.

00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:05.710
It depends on how strong your feelings are.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:12.250
When you were on the radio,

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:16.230
we could sense the confidence you've built up from doing Aikatsu every day.

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:18.230
<i>That's</i> why your aura appeared.

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:31.980
Be proud of yourself.

00:17:43.190 --> 00:17:46.200
That's why I'm sure that if you 
continue doing the things you like,

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:48.910
you're sure to find your own dream.

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:53.210
That's right!

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:57.680
Ah, it's Hoshimiya Ichigo!

00:18:04.590 --> 00:18:08.930
<i>My daily Aikatsu and trying hard in my own way.</i>

00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:11.390
<i>That's</i> my<i> aura.</i>

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:21.490
<i>Right. If I just do my best I can turn even these uneventful days into something special.</i>

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:25.680
That was amazing, Nee-san and Ran-san!

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:27.300
Thanks.

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:32.010
And Onee-chan, I thought you were 
like a real idol back there.

00:21:32.530 --> 00:21:34.310
That's the first time you've said that to me!

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:37.180
And also... thank you.

00:21:37.180 --> 00:21:38.100
Why?

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:41.320
You answered my worries on the radio show.

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:46.380
Remember? Raichingale was... me.

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:48.450
That was <i>you</i>?!

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:56.080
I shouldn't have said that!

00:22:00.520 --> 00:22:04.590
It seems like their concert went off without a hitch.

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:08.290
I'm glad. I hope Hoshimiya, Kiriya, and Shibuki

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:10.770
will continue ramping up their Aikatsu from now on.

00:22:10.770 --> 00:22:14.460
It's almost time for Shibuki to face her fateful battle.

00:22:15.870 --> 00:22:18.380
Her beloved brand,

00:22:18.380 --> 00:22:21.850
Spicy Ageha, is about to hold it's Representative Audition.

00:23:55.670 --> 00:23:57.740
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:58.630 --> 00:24:00.940
Does having to disguise myself when I go outside

00:24:00.940 --> 00:24:03.010
mean that I'm a celebrity now?

00:24:03.010 --> 00:24:04.260
Those who wish to be idols

00:24:04.260 --> 00:24:07.420
must have good sense when it comes to picking disguises.

00:24:07.810 --> 00:24:09.880
Carefully choose your disguise.

00:24:10.750 --> 00:24:14.900
I can't afford to fail Spicy Ageha's Representative Audition.

00:24:14.900 --> 00:24:17.800
But I won't be able to be a Muse with just perfection.

00:24:17.800 --> 00:24:18.960
"Muse"?

00:24:18.960 --> 00:24:20.500
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:20.500 --> 00:24:21.720
The Muse of Ageha.

00:24:21.720 --> 00:24:23.970
Always passionate, Idol Activities!
